    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0494" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/3504: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-31T17:00:00-06:00">December 31, 1942—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1250. Embassy’s telegram No. 1243, December 30, 7 p.m.<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d417-f1"/> The Foreign Office has issued a statement containing the
                    text of the exchange of notes<anchor n="52" xml:id="d417-f2"/> between
                        Padilla<anchor n="53" xml:id="d417-f3"/> and Sikorski<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d417-f4"/> regarding a limited arrangement for the admission of
                    Polish refugees to Mexico. The number of Poles accepted will be in accordance
                    with the capacity of the country.</p>
                <p>Transportation to Mexico will be without expense to the Mexican Government.
                    Expenses of their sojourn will be borne by the Polish Government. Repatriation
                    at the expense of the Polish Government will take place at the first propitious
                    moment after the [war]. Poles while in Mexico will be distributed where they can
                    contribute to the economy of Mexico without [conflicting] with Mexican
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>Texts of the notes will be forwarded by airmail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Messersmith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
